 ('p', 'The arithmetic of tipping and splitting is the easy part; the social choreography is what people actually find awkward. A few habits smooth it over. The most effective is to agree the approach before the bill arrives, an even split or paying for your own, so there is no negotiation over a table of finished plates. When splitting evenly, rounding up slightly to a convenient number per person avoids fishing for small change and tends to leave a marginally more generous tip, which no one minds. If one person puts the whole bill on their card for the group to repay, working out each share clearly and sending it promptly keeps things fair and friendly.'),
